From: EglantinePS5 <noreply@eglantineps5.local>
Subject: [PATCH] texture_cache: do not upload an image with no CPU backing

RefreshContents uploads when an image is CPU-modified, reading the guest range at image.gpu_addr.
When that range has no CPU mapping - ImageCpuAddress above made a stand-in address for it - the read
falls through to DeviceMemoryManager's unmapped path, which zero-fills and logs "Unmapped Device
ReadBlock". A 445-second Ocarina session did that seventeen times in one burst, and the burst
followed the discovery of new 3D images (64x64x64, 64x36x96, 128x72x96), not the feedback-loop copy
(it is a GPU-to-GPU vkCmdCopyImage).

Skipping the upload is what the case requires: there is nothing to read, and uploading zeroes over
what the GPU already wrote is worse than keeping it. Sparse images upload tile by tile elsewhere and
are left alone.

What this can break: an image whose bytes exist only in guest memory the CPU cannot see keeps its
previous host contents instead of becoming zeroes. If such an image is actually needed, it can show
stale or wrong texels. That is the same class of error the zero-fill produced, and it is confined to
whole-image uploads of non-sparse images with no CPU mapping at all.

Checked: applies to the tree the 0410-0414 stack produces. Not run on a console.

diff --git a/src/video_core/texture_cache/texture_cache.h b/src/video_core/texture_cache/texture_cache.h
--- a/src/video_core/texture_cache/texture_cache.h
+++ b/src/video_core/texture_cache/texture_cache.h
@@ -2131,6 +2131,19 @@
         // Only upload modified images
         return;
     }
+    // A GPU address with no CPU mapping has nothing to upload from: the read falls through to the
+    // unmapped path, which zero-fills and logs "Unmapped Device ReadBlock". Ocarina's newly
+    // discovered 3D images did that in bursts of seventeen. Sparse images upload tile by tile
+    // elsewhere, so only this whole-image path is skipped.
+    const bool sparse_upload =
+        True(image.flags & (ImageFlagBits::SparseLayers | ImageFlagBits::SparseTiles));
+    if (!sparse_upload && !gpu_memory->GpuToCpuAddress(image.gpu_addr, image.guest_size_bytes)) {
+        image.flags &= ~ImageFlagBits::CpuModified;
+        if (False(image.flags & ImageFlagBits::Tracked)) {
+            TrackImage(image, image_id);
+        }
+        return;
+    }
     VideoCommon::Nx2Profile::Scope profile_scope{VideoCommon::Nx2Profile::Zone::TextureUpload};
 
     image.flags &= ~ImageFlagBits::CpuModified;
